Linux-Networking-for-Devops


Network:
     A computer network formed when two or more computers are connected in some way, to share information or resources more broadly. 
A network is the interconnection of computing devices, from computers, to phones, to printers to smart devices and so on


Network are typically made up of servers and clients:

Client-Server model: 
     This model, user devices or client, connect via to a network with centrally located server to get the resources they need.


A Server:
     is a large-capacity computer that contains the hard drives, printers and resources that are shared with other computers on a network
server are designed to be able to handel more intensive workload that a personal computer can.Personal computer could run server process 
but would not be able to handle the waste and crash


Client: 
     are other computers and devices on a network that request and receive resources from servers. Example end-user devices like phones 
and personal computers


Private network:- 
     A private network excludes unauthorised users from joining network. An example is an intranet. A network where the connection is between 
devices within a particular setting.


Public network:- 
     The public internet is also type of network. It is a global of other networks, allowing for worldwide sharing of information.
Since it is accessible to public, the internet is an example public network.
